    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d459-a1">

                <pb facs="0744" n="616" xml:id="pg616"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 28.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Police order in the subprefecture and administration
                        of police</hi>.</head>
                <p>A gratification will be given of from 50 to 1,000 silver soles to every one who
                    gives opportune notice, with all the necessary and exact details, about anything
                    that will contribute to the better service of the police. Said notice may be
                    verbal or in writing, and strict secrecy is guaranteed, as also that the
                    gratification will be given into the hands of the adviser, or in the way he
                    indicates in the notice of accusation.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1885-08-20"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">20th August</hi>,
                    1885</date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
